  "title": "Job Architecture Is the Foundation Nobody Built. AI Is Finally Making It Fixable.",
  "summary": "Ask most HR leaders whether their company has a job architecture and they'll say yes. Ask them to pull it up and you'll get a pause. Somewhere there's a spreadsheet. Or a deck from a consultant engagement three years ago. Or a framework that was built for one part of the org and never extended to the rest. It exists technically. But it isn't working. And almost every compensation problem traces back to this.",
